      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#1 · Pseudo-Apollodorus, Library 3.14.1 (Frazer digital text, q001)",
          "title": "Claim, witness, verdict",
          "italic": "The sequence demonstrates adjudication with its parts held apart: the divine arbiters are distinct from the king's witnessing, and the testimony to the planting is the award's stated ground.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "Cecrops, first king of Attica, a son of the soil compounded of man and serpent, has already given the country formerly called Acte his name. The gods seek cities for peculiar worship. Poseidon arrives first and strikes the middle of the Acropolis with his trident, producing the sea called Erechtheis. Athena arrives after him, calls Cecrops to witness her act of taking",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "possession, and plants an olive tree. The two strive; Zeus separates them and appoints arbiters — the twelve gods in this version. The country is awarded to Athena because Cecrops bears witness that she planted the olive; she names the city Athens after herself. The selected text keeps the arbiters distinct from the witnessing: this is not the king choosing a favourite gift.\n\nOccurrences: Cecrops's naming and double nature (#0–#1); the trident-strike and Erechtheis (#1); the witnessed planting (#1, #4); the twelve arbiters and testimony (#1); the naming of Athens (#1).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
