      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#2 · Herodotus 8.55; Pausanias 1.26.5–7 and 1.27.2; the Acropolis Museum's Erechtheion account",
          "title": "The sanctuary remembers both claims",
          "italic": "The material relation demonstrates the retained contrary: the victorious civic form keeps the counter-claim inside its sacred architecture.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The Erechtheion's eastern room was dedicated to Athena, while its lower western room accommodated shrines including Poseidon-Erechtheus; the complex incorporated the contest's sacred signs — Athena's olive, Poseidon's trident marks in the bedrock, the spring of salty water. Herodotus reports the Athenians describing olive and sea as the gods' witnesses in Erechtheus's sanctuary, and the olive's regrowth after burning — a shoot about a cubit long on the",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "very day. Pausanias gives altars for Poseidon with Erechtheus, Butes and Hephaestus, the sea-water cistern whose wave sounds in a south wind, the trident mark, and a two-cubit regrowth on the day of burning — a distinct report from Herodotus's. The oil-fed lamp he describes is a separate cultic object, not evidence for a root-to-light chain in the source. The sacred place retains the rival signs; their coexistence is the material relation Taylor receives.\n\nOccurrences: the double shrine (#2); the olive's burning and regrowth in two reports (#2); the trident mark and salt spring (#2); the lamp kept distinct (#2).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
